--- body ---
## Context

Spinoff identified 2026-06-05 from two converging lines of evidence: the
PR #289 architecture panel (4 independent reviewers) and a deep-research
report (docs/research/agnostic-reviewer-landscape.md, 28 sources / 25
adversarially-verified claims). Both reached the same conclusion: the
verify external-reviewer panel (0205) should NOT be built as a bespoke
ACP client. No single existing tool delivers the full stack
(decorrelated panel + read-only containment + normalized findings), and
ACP/A2A capability grants + agent "modes" (aider --ask) are
COOPERATIVE-only — a misbehaving or prompt-injected reviewer bypasses
them. Genuine containment is OS-level (Seatbelt/bubblewrap), and even
that leaks secrets by default (credential files readable, allowlist
without TLS inspection permits domain-fronting exfil).

The reusable, generalizable unit underneath the panel is therefore a
**sandbox-runner + output-normalizer**: a small tool that turns ANY
agnostic CLI agent (aider --ask, PR-Agent, gemini, codex, a thin
OpenAI-compatible caller) into an OS-contained, read-only reviewer seat
emitting normalized findings. This is broader than verify's internal
plumbing (0216 stays Claude-native) and is the natural spinoff.

## Relation to existing tickets

- Supersedes the ACP-keystone framing of 0207 (thin agent) and 0208
  (ACP client harness): ACP becomes OPTIONAL plumbing, the OS sandbox
  becomes the load-bearing requirement.
- Feeds 0205 (panel contract/decorrelation rule) as the seat mechanism.
- Gated by the open decorrelation question (deep-research wbclco9po):
  how many seats are worth running is unproven; do not scale N before
  that evidence lands.

## Actions (scoping — refine before execution)

1. Seat-runner: launch a reviewer CLI inside an OS sandbox
   (bubblewrap on Linux) with: read-only repo bind, scoped denyRead on
   credential/secret paths (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, bash-env.sh, ~/.claude
   memory), and network isolation (deny by default; allow only the one
   model endpoint host the seat needs).
2. Per-seat credential scoping: construct a MINIMAL child env (only the
   one API key that seat needs; strip BASH_ENV so the child does not
   re-source the full secret file). Addresses PR #289 red-team MAJOR.
3. Output normalizer: parse each agent's output (free text / JSON) into
   the 0205 contract shape (severity + file:line + rationale); a finding
   that does not parse is surfaced as WARN, never silently dropped.
   Quantify per-agent normalization reliability (deep-research open gap).
4. Per-seat fail-open + timeout: one seat hanging or erroring must WARN
   and continue, never ESCALATE the whole verify run.
5. Pick a first agnostic seat (aider --ask or a thin OpenAI-compatible
   caller) and smoke it end-to-end inside the sandbox on one merged PR.

## Test

Seat-runner test: a seat that attempts a repo write is BLOCKED by the
sandbox (not merely by the agent's mode); a seat that attempts to read a
denyRead'd credential path is denied; a seat whose endpoint is
unreachable fails loud; the normalizer turns canned agent output into a
valid findings file and surfaces an unparseable finding as WARN.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Seat-runner launches a CLI reviewer under an OS sandbox: read-only repo, denyRead on secrets, network deny-by-default
- [ ] Repo-write and credential-read attempts BLOCKED at the OS layer (test proves it, not the agent's cooperative mode)
- [ ] Per-seat minimal-env credential scoping (BASH_ENV stripped from child)
- [ ] Output normalizer to the 0205 contract shape; unparseable findings WARN, not dropped
- [ ] Per-seat fail-open + timeout; one seat's failure never ESCALATEs verify
- [ ] One agnostic seat smoke-tested end-to-end on a real PR
